# fixedbugs, defect 643, lane b21-win, 2026-10-11, the twin on a header of the
# program's own of the Windows surface row *one C symbol carries two
# bindings, in two modules*, which the CI's Windows leg read red (defect 640).
#
# The header gives `abs` a C99 inline definition, which provides no external
# definition (C11 6.7.4p7), and two modules bind it. clang's dump of the
# header list holds its own implicit declaration of the builtin `abs`, marked
# `extern`, before the header's, and that one was read as the program's: the
# definition read external, and the program was refused `ffi_defined_twice`
# at exit 1, a correct program refused on every platform. An implicit
# declaration is clang's, and is not read.
use fixedbugs643/other

extern "fixedbugs-643-an-inline-abs.h"
    function abs(x: i32) -> i32

function main()
    print(abs(x: -3))
    print(other.magnitude(x: -4))
